        "Content": "The Glebe,  Donegal Town  F94 TDK7\r\n\r\nDetached Residence    \r\n“Cois Farraige”\r\n\r\nTruly Magnificent Setting Overlooking & Extending to Donegal Bay\r\n\r\nSituate in a quiet residential cul de sac,  opposite the Abbey Vocational School and only 650 metres from The Diamond.  Occupying an elevated setting enjoying exceptional views of Donegal Estuary.    Constructed in 1984 and extending to 219.77 sq.m. , comprising -\r\n\r\nGround Floor.\tLarge Entrance Hallway, Sitting Room,  Dining Room,  Living \t\t\t\tRoom/Study, Kitchen, Living Room,  1 No. Bedroom & Bathroom;\r\n\r\nFirst Floor.\t\t3 No. Bedrooms (1 en-suite)\r\n\r\nFront Garden extending to sea;  private garden at rear\t\t\t\r\n\r\nEntrance Porch\t\t3.65 m.  x  1.07 m.\r\n\t\t\t\ttiled floor\r\n\r\nHallway\t\t\t5.01 m.  x  4.02 m.\r\n\t\t\t\tsolid maple floor\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSitting Room\t\t4.86 m.  x  4.84 m.\r\n\t\t\t\tsolid maple floor; three windows overlooking Bay;  corner \t\t\t\tfireplace,  internal door to -\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDining Room\t\t4.86 m.  x  3.90 m.\r\n\t\t\t\tsolid maple floor; corner fireplace with ceiling high stone \t\t\t\t\tfire surround with enclosed solid fuel stove\r\n\r\n  \r\n\r\nConservatory\t\t3.98 m.  x  2.39 m.\r\ntiled floor\r\n\r\n\r\nKitchen\t\t\t5.00 m.  x  3.59 m.\r\n\t\t\t\tfitted units,  hotpress,  laminated flooring; overlooking rear \t\t\t\tpaved \tpatio \r\n\r\n  \r\n\r\nUtility\t\t\t\t3.06 m.  x  2.42 m.\r\n\t\t\t\tfitted unit and counter;  door to rear patio\r\n\r\nLiving Room / Day Room\t4.86 m.  x  3.93 m.\r\n\t\t\t\tcathedral high ceiling;  solid maple floor,  french doors to \t\t\t\t\tside\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLiving Room / Study\t3.72 m.  x  3.62 m.\r\nsolid maple floor; overlooking Bay;  currently used for \t\tLiving area but ideal for home office\r\n\r\n    \r\n\r\nBedroom No. 1\t\t3.61 m.  x  3.58 m.\r\n\t\t\t\tlaminated floor; wall length built-in wardrobes\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBathroom\t\t\t3.60 m.  x  2.42 m.\r\n\t\t\t\tBath, separate walk-in shower, toilet and wash basin;  tiled \t\t\t\tfloor, surrounding shower and lower walls\r\n\r\n  \r\n\r\nFirst Floor.\r\n\r\nLanding\t\t\tCarpet flooring\r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom No. 2\t\t4.44 m.  x  4.07 m.  two windows with views of Bay\r\n\t\r\nWalk-in wardrobe\t2.35 m.  x  1.67 m.\r\n\r\n\tEn-suite\tElectric shower, toilet and wash basin; tiled floor and \t\t\t\t\taround shower; velox window\r\n\r\n   \r\n\r\nBedroom No. 3\t\t4.04 m.  x  2.34 m.\r\n\t\t\t\tCarpet\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom No. 4\t\t4.88 m.  x  3.63 m.\r\n\t\t\t\tcarpet,  window overlooking Bay; built in storage closets -  \t\t\t\tample room to construct en-suite\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBer No : 118649664\r\nOil fired central heating\tMains sewerage\r\n\r\nRear Paved Patio area -  7.31 m.  x  3.34 m.  enjoying morning and afternoon sun\r\n\r\nTo the rear is a private enclosed lawn, further lawns to front – both sides of road , lower side extends to sea\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAnderson Auctioneers for itself and as agent for the vendor gives notice that:\r\n\r\nThese particulars are only a general outline for the guidance of intending purchasers or lessees and do not constitute in whole or in part, an offer or a Contract.\r\n\r\nAny intending purchaser or lessee should satisfy themselves by inspection, searches, inquiries, and survey as to the correctness of each statement.\r\n\r\n[OR] Whilst every care has been taken in the preparation of these particulars, and they are believed to be correct, they are not warranted and intending purchasers/lessees should satisfy themselves as to the correctness of the information given.\r\n\r\nAll statements in these particulars are made on the without responsibility part of Anderson Auctioneers or the vendor \r\n\r\nNo statement in these particulars is to be relied upon as a statement or representation of fact.\r\n\r\nNeither Anderson Auctioneers nor anyone in its employment or acting on its behalf has authority to make any representation or warranty in relation to this property.\r\n\r\nNothing in these particulars shall be deemed to be a statement that the property is in good repair or condition or otherwise nor that any services or facilities are in good working order.\r\n\r\nPhotographs may show only certain parts and aspects of the property at the time when the photographs were taken and you should rely upon actual inspection.\r\n\r\nNo assumption should be made in respect of parts of the property not shown in photographs.\r\n\r\nAny areas, measurements, or distances are only approximate.\r\n\r\nAny reference to alterations or use is not intended to be a statement that any necessary planning, building regulation, listed building or any other consent has been obtained."
